# Prada L'Homme Intense-inspired — Floral Iris / Tonka Interior — Astra V2-B18

**Date:** 2026-09-05
**Claim mode:** named_reference
**Reference contract:** prada_lhomme_intense
**Reference scope:** architecture
**Status:** FULLY SPECIFIED DEVELOPMENT HYPOTHESIS / HOLD FOR EXECUTION AND RELEASE

This is the source-preserving candidate selected for the next controlled test, not an established improvement, proprietary recreation, absolute Astra ceiling, or physical compounding authorization. Structured source: docs/research/Prada_LHomme_Intense_Astra_V2_accounting.json. Only OpenAI-native reasoning was used. One read-only Astra challenge was requested at the host's `ultra` setting and completed; the collaboration receipt does not attest the executed effort. The parent selected doses and verified arithmetic locally.

## 1. What actually changed

The intended object is a floral iris exterior opening onto a warmer tonka-sandalwood interior, with patchouli giving a dark boundary. This is a relationship to test, not a claim that the mixture already smells that way. Reduce broad support and optional accents together while increasing tonka/sandalwood responsibility. It is not an addition-only intensification.

The official product and campaign place iris, amber, patchouli and tonka in the Intense identity, with sandalwood and roasted tonka in the product notes. The campaign's floral-iris/airy-tonka juxtaposition motivates B. Neither inspected page establishes leather as an anchor or discloses the commercial composition. [Prada product](https://www.prada.com/ww/en/p/lhomme-prada-intense-edp-100-ml/2A1252_2HC1_F0Z99_P_ML100), [Prada campaign](https://www.prada.com/us/en/pradasphere/fragrances/la-femme-et-l-homme-prada/la-femme-et-l-homme-prada-intense.html), accessed 2026-09-05.

Protected: floral iris; dry amber/patchouli contrast; rounded but non-pastry tonka; sandalwood continuity. Reject a shift toward berry-violet candy, vanilla dessert, tobacco-led wood, overt suede, smoky oud, blue freshness or laundry musk. The original Prada reference contract is NOT an Intense truth test.

