These are mass allocations, not smell shares or optimized target ratios. The whole V2 master has LESS supplied fragrant product than V1 (3579.5 versus 3808 mg). Equal concentrate volume or equal master mass would confound a controlled comparison; Section 8 removes that known loading confound.

## 2. Independent TARGET / IDEAL

The ideal is a functional product-selection specification, not the current stock formula normalized. It allows an assay-characterized orris, selected iris and sandalwood grades, a patchouli fraction, and a characterized amber-tonka reconstruction even where the current build uses approximations. No purchase is implied. Owning a material does not qualify it as the ideal.

Joint exploratory envelopes in ppm w/w of a carrier-excluded supplied-product pool: floral iris 320000–420000; amber-tonka interior 130000–220000 (including the woody-amber junction when assigned there); patchouli contrast 50000–90000; sandalwood connection 100000–160000; space/separation/finish 190000–300000. Select jointly to 1000000 ppm; boundaries are design hypotheses, not published Prada proportions, safe-use limits, or validated performance ranges. Borderline optional seams occupy the applicable parent module, not a new budget.

The following 18 source-linked ideal decisions remain separately visible; optional means testable, not already proven unnecessary. No source identity or function is silently deleted.

| ID | Ideal function | Product class / option set | Target-linked selection criterion | Current build candidate | Mapping gap / independent alternative |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| I01 | Iris body | AIMI / floral methylionone grade | A floral-orris body with restrained berry character; compare grade-specific samples, not trade-name prestige. | Alpha Isomethyl Ionone | Grade and isomer distribution unverified |
| I02 | Specific iris accent | Assay-described irone material | Separately adjustable irone accent, not simply more violet body. | Alpha Irone | Owned alpha-irone stock is not a verified optimum isomer blend |
| I03 | Root texture | Characterized orris product | Root texture that does not require camphor or heavy lipstick. | Orris Liquid | PW supplied-product identity/assay gap; no natural-extract assumption |
| I04 | Petal approach | Selected ionone grade | A floral entry into the iris, without a berry-violet theme. | Alpha Ionone | Compare against more iris body at common product budget |
| I05 | Dry root contour | Dry orris ketone, optional | Contour distinct from root texture, not duplicate earthiness. | Orivone | Strongest alternative is controlled omission, not an assumed equivalent |
| I06 | Rounded tonka | Characterized coumarinic-tonka reconstruction | A rounded warm interior that remains airy rather than pastry-like. | Tonkarome | Opaque product; known dilution does not establish contents |
| I07 | Dry tonka definition | Coumarin or a characterized dry-tonka product | Independent dry hay definition, with sweetness assessed jointly with tonka body. | Coumarin | Planned weighed stock; existing unknown-basis stock excluded |
| I08 | Almond-powder junction | Piperonal-class accent, optional | A small iris-tonka connection that does not become heliotrope. | Heliotropal | Unverified air ODT; omission must be separate from other accents |
| I09 | Dry amber contour | Ambroxide-class or characterized amber material | Dry amber continuation distinct from sweet resinous warmth. | Ambrox Super | Broad amber meaning not fully represented by this one product |
| I10 | Patchouli shadow | Chosen whole oil or characterized patchouli fraction | Woody depth/earth/camphor balance chosen for iris contrast. | Patchouli EO | Whole oil is an approximation, not an ideal requirement |
| I11 | Sandalwood connection | Selected sandalwood grade or minimal distinct-role accord | Cream and grain connecting iris to tonka without a new loud wood theme. | Bacdanol | Ebanol/Sandalore are alternatives, not equal-strength replacements |
| I12 | Woody junction | Woody-amber/tobacco or dry-woody connector | Connect the floral subject to amber, without tobacco takeover. | Kephalis | Vertofix-class route is a different design option |
| I13 | Textile grain | Textural woody material, optional | Grain distinguishable from generic woody volume. | Cashmeran | Retained source function; necessity unproved |
| I14 | Suede seam | Controlled suede product, optional | A subordinate seam with no independent leather theme. | Suederal | Not an official Intense anchor; isolate omission first |
| I15 | Floral space | Selected methyl dihydrojasmonate grade | Access around iris and warm interior rather than an independent floral lead. | Hedione | HC is a grade-change hypothesis, not automatic improvement |
| I16 | Woody separation | Selected transparent woody-amber grade | Distance/contour between subject and interior, not louder generic woods. | Iso E Super | Alternative grades require matched-context comparison |
| I17 | Cosmetic interface | Salicylate-type cushion, optional | A specific cosmetic iris-to-sandalwood boundary distinct from musk rounding. | Benzyl Salicylate | Benzyl Benzoate is a vehicle/control option, not an odor-equivalent replacement |
| I18 | Single musk finish | One selected macrocyclic or other target-matched musk | Rounding that leaves iris and warm interior legible. | Ambrettolide | EB, Exaltolide and Habanolide are alternatives; no automatic chord |

The strongest unresolved design choices are the exact iris-body grade, one versus two root articulators, the tonka body/definition coupling, and the meaning of amber beyond ambroxide. V2 is a source-preserving realization of B, not proof that all 18 current products are indispensable.

