Future preparation specifications, not completed work: PLI-PREP-C20 = 2.000 g Coumarin supplied powder + 8.000 g DEP; PLI-PREP-H10 = 1.000 g neat Heliotropal + 9.000 g DEP. Require appropriate handling review, exact preparation IDs/labels, logged masses and demonstrated homogeneous usable condition. Do not assume solubility or stability. Do not add heat or another solvent without an explicitly revised preparation. No inventories were edited to record these proposed stocks as existing.

The smallest master transfer is 20 mg. Balance uncertainty must be appropriate to that transfer (e.g. at most 0.2 mg for a 1% target), or scale the WHOLE master and document it. Display readability is not verified uncertainty. These weighed instructions do not authorize a sub-10-µL neat transfer.

## 6. Nominal 30 mL / 20% finish

Six grams is not six millilitres. After resolving execution prerequisites, obtain a measured 6.00 mL homogeneous concentrate aliquot at a recorded temperature, then use the verified ethanol product q.s. to final 30.00 mL. A larger proportional master may be needed to obtain the aliquot. Record its mass m6 and the final mass M.

For each material: finished supplied-product ppm w/w = `m6_g * (product_mg / 6000) / M_g * 1000000`. Unknown m6/M means actual finished ppm remains UNKNOWN. This convention is neither 20% w/w nor 20% pure odorants. Do not simply add a presumed 24.00 mL ethanol and claim the final volume.

No bottle has been prepared, no skin use authorized, and no stability/safety/remaining-stock-quantity verification completed.

## 7. Three independently challenged directions

| Direction | Question | Parent decision / principal risk |
|---|---|---|
| A — ten-product identity control | Can iris/amber/patchouli/tonka/sandalwood carry the object without the eight articulating/support rows? | Exact paper control below, NOT promoted as equal-complexity successor. Risk: broad, flat iris-to-wood transition. |
| B — floral iris / tonka interior | Does lowering general support while strengthening tonka-sandalwood reveal the intended inner warmth without losing floral iris? | Selected source-preserving V2-B18 for first comparison. Risk: soft-focus powder, sweet violet and a blurred warm interior. |
| C — rooted iris / darker amber-patchouli | Does a small characterized balsamic contribution make amber more than an ambroxide outline? | Independent ideal candidate; raw stock mapping blocked by unresolved resin product/basis. Risk: resin, tobacco and generic sweet-amber drift. No fictitious resin dose from current stock. |

The worker favored B, then C, with A most informative as a control. Parent accepted that ordering as design rationale, NOT observed superiority. The worker suggested omitting Orivone, Cashmeran, Suederal and Heliotropal in B. Parent retained reduced, explicit source functions and made that deletion a separately recorded test arm. No evidence yet adjudicates the deleted module or any one member.

