## 10. Diagnostic model and independent scientific interpretation

Existing CLI and formatter only; no shared physics, stock pins, parser code or release rules were edited. The input coordinate is `raw_mg / repository_material_density`, so multiplication inside the existing model exactly reconstructs supplied-product grams. This is an algebraic adapter, NOT a stock-density measurement. V2's 6109.667348668188 coordinate units are not 6109.667 real microlitres.

Known carriers are included alongside a hypothetical 24 g of 96% w/w ethanol/water. The resulting 30 g scenario is not the actual 30 mL bottle. Matrix authority stays `declared_volume_proxy`. Fixed-mass exactness does not make gamma, VP, mixture composition, ODT or evaporation experimentally correct.

A first run was preserved under output/prada_lhomme_intense_astra_v2/run1. It did not recognize the artifact text `neat / as supplied`, causing 15 stock failures. The final artifact uses parser-supported `neat`; all 18 declared stock specifications parse. The single corrective rerun changes no dose, property or matrix and reduces those stock failures to the five genuine unresolved runtime bindings.

The immediate unchanged V1 mass recipe was supplied through a separately hash-bound, mass-faithful parent representation using the same matrix scenario. G15/pre-mix reports PASS with parent and temporal comparisons available. That is a model-coordinate arithmetic screen, not physical release.

Read the full headspace table and five windows in the verbatim outputs below before gate decisions. The final table predicts opening total vapor 0.174760 ppm; active-note T/H/B 0/62.4/37.6 and modeled OAV-weighted split 0/86.2/13.8. These distributions are different quantities. The claimed skin context in the legacy simulator is not skin authorization.

### Decision-changing data limits

- Bacdanol: IFF reports VP 0.001065 mmHg at 23 C (about 0.14199 Pa), versus local 0.001 Pa. [IFF Bacdanol](https://www.iff.com/scent/ingredients-compendium/bacdanol/).
- Ambrettolide: IFF reports 0.000158 mmHg at 23 C (about 0.021065 Pa), versus local 0.003 Pa. [IFF Ambrettolide](https://www.iff.com/scent/ingredients-compendium/ambrettolide/).
- Orivone: IFF reports 0.031743 mmHg at 23 C (about 4.23205 Pa), versus local 8.6 Pa, and describes a camphoraceous/earthy orris character. [IFF Orivone](https://www.iff.com/scent/ingredients-compendium/orivone/).
- These supplier values are different-temperature, product-transfer SENSITIVITY inputs, not replacements for owned-lot data. Gamma and ODT remain fixed only for an explicitly one-factor stress test.
- Heliotropal's local 0.006 ppb air ODT cites a compilation but no primary air experiment was established in the bounded search. Orivone is explicitly UNVERIFIED in the repository's ODT metadata. No new threshold is invented; high ranking is not an aesthetic veto.
- Patchouli composite coverage is partial and not a lot analysis. The Orris Liquid decomposition is not proof that the owned PW product has that natural profile. Tonkarome and Suederal are not justified as single pure molecular species.
- Gamma is heuristic or transferred for every material; a value of one is not observed ideal behavior. Iso E's modeled gamma near 8.69 materially affects its ranking.
- The formatter's receptor-cap rationale, natural-complexity percentage, Tonkarome glycoside claim, skin transformations and price-tier suggestions are not accepted as material-specific scientific conclusions. Legacy blanket concentration-basis warnings also conflict with the verified stock parser declarations; preserve them as integration issues, not missing physical labels.
- The engine still applies an original-Prada fallback after the explicit unknown Intense contract. Do not add neroli/geranium/pepper to satisfy that wrong reference. The missing specific contract remains a real HOLD.
- Sub-threshold screening for Bacdanol, Ambrettolide, Kephalis, Orris and Suederal prompts specific data/omission checks; it does not prove that they cannot contribute. Benzyl Salicylate's matrix/cushion hypothesis is separately testable, not a free exemption.
- Gate IFRA/allergen warnings are incomplete and internally inconsistent; nine missing limits prevent a safety determination. No label, safety or stability conclusion is made from this report.

### Bounded sensitivity result

Frozen-composition/gamma/ODT VP substitutions give Bacdanol OAV 0.003145 to 0.446591; Ambrettolide 0.132874 to 0.932992; Orivone 74.820707 to 36.819200. These are different-temperature source-transfer scenarios, not corrected truth. Bacdanol and Ambrettolide still do not establish above-threshold contribution in this scenario; their retention is a functional hypothesis requiring comparison, not validation by the supplier page. Full numbers: output/prada_lhomme_intense_astra_v2/sensitivity.json.

Heliotropal ODT stress factors 0.1/1/10/100/1000 give OAV 2067.23/206.72/20.67/2.067/0.207 at otherwise fixed inputs. The factors are hypothetical stress cases, NOT uncertainty intervals or alternative literature thresholds. This demonstrates why an unverified threshold must not decide its aesthetic role.

The target-neutral deep-plane compatibility check completed with gate PASS and overall HOLD. All 13 plane statuses are WITHHELD and every authority flag is false. Inspect output/prada_lhomme_intense_astra_v2/deep_plane.json. A completed check is not a completed perfume validation.

Post-model survival: Bacdanol/Ambrettolide/Kephalis/Orris Liquid/Suederal are DATA HOLD and NON-INFORMATIVE AS COMPUTATIONAL PROOF of their proposed character role; the proposed sensory tests are not guaranteed to yield detectable effects. Heliotropal and Orivone retain ODT DATA HOLD despite their high rankings. Tonkarome and Patchouli retain MIXTURE/LOT DATA HOLD. Benzyl Salicylate is a STRUCTURAL HYPOTHESIS requiring its own omission comparison. The remaining eight rows are retained as untested design hypotheses, not accepted sensory contributors. None is increased merely to overcome an uncertain threshold.

Focused verification receipt: output/prada_lhomme_intense_astra_v2/verification_receipt.json covers arithmetic, exact predecessor preservation, parser declarations, model-mass consistency, comparison carrier matching, verbatim report embedding, raw data coverage, and tracked-file preservation. It is not a full project release verification or a safety assessment.

### Parent's perfumer interpretation (hypotheses, not an observed smell)

1. Character: floral iris contrasted with dry amber-patchouli and a more legible tonka-sandalwood interior. It remains an Intense-inspired study, not a base-Prada or Dior copy.
2. Opening: the model strongly weights Iso E/Hedione, with a highly threshold-sensitive Heliotropal signal. Whether floral iris is actually the exterior is the first blind question. Total modeled vapor is 0.174760 ppm; no perceived shares are inferred.
3. Heart: the model changes little by 30 min. It does NOT demonstrate that the desired warmer interior becomes accessible. Record iris continuity and warm-interior access separately.
4. Drydown: 37.9% base in the modeled active-note distribution is not base smell dominance. Determine whether tonka/sandalwood retain an iris trace rather than replacing it.
5. Sillage/diffusion: no calibrated spatial prediction. The Iso E/Hedione ranking is a possible screening concern with high gamma uncertainty, not measured projection.
6. Longevity: the about 0.9% modeled loss index is not evaporation data or hours on skin. Physical persistence remains NOT TESTED.
7. Balance: the support allocation is reduced deliberately; sigma-log about 1.52 is a contrast descriptor, not quality. Carrier-matched comparison is required before calling the structure clearer.
8. Flags: disputed optional accents; unverified root and proprietary product composition; supplier VP disagreement; unverified thresholds; incomplete safety and runtime stock authority.

